<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Maximus, Metropolitan of Kiev</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1305</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Maximus, Metropolitan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyiv">Kiev</a>, was a Greek churchman who headed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-orthodox-church">Orthodox Church</a> of Rus' as Metropolitan of Kiev and all Rus' from 1283 to 1305. After Kiev was devastated by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a>, he moved the seat of the metropolitan to Vladimir in 1299, bringing the head of the Russian church to the north-east. His successors later moved it on to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a>.</p></div>
